1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:02,599
December 8, 2017.

2
00:00:02,599 --> 00:00:06,830
A 2010 Ford Focus with Baja California plates

3
00:00:06,830 --> 00:00:10,685
waits in line to enter the United States.

4
00:00:11,135 --> 00:00:14,150
A Customs and Border Protection officer walks

5
00:00:14,150 --> 00:00:15,557
the lanes with a dog.

6
00:00:15,557 --> 00:00:18,303
Near the car's rear door, the dog alerts.

7
00:00:18,753 --> 00:00:19,944
The driver is 19.

8
00:00:19,944 --> 00:00:23,447
He tells the officer he's going to an outlet mall.

9
00:00:23,897 --> 00:00:27,065
In secondary inspection, officers pull apart

10
00:00:27,065 --> 00:00:30,378
the rear seats, both quarter panels, a speaker

11
00:00:30,378 --> 00:00:33,043
box, and the firewall under the hood.

12
00:00:33,043 --> 00:00:34,627
They find 31 packages.

13
00:00:35,077 --> 00:00:37,484
About 77 pounds of fentanyl.

14
00:00:37,484 --> 00:00:41,180
In court records, an expert estimates it at

15
00:00:41,180 --> 00:00:43,931
800,000 potentially fatal doses.

16
00:00:44,381 --> 00:00:46,700
How does a drug this deadly cross at the

17
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:49,251
busiest land port in the Western Hemisphere?

18
00:00:49,251 --> 00:00:51,165
And what does it take to stop it?

19
00:00:51,765 --> 00:00:54,794
This is the case of fentanyl at San Ysidro.

20
00:00:57,394 --> 00:01:01,127
San Ysidro is where Interstate 5 meets Mexico.

21
00:01:01,577 --> 00:01:03,180
On one side, San Diego.

22
00:01:03,180 --> 00:01:04,713
On the other, Tijuana.

23
00:01:04,713 --> 00:01:07,849
The port sits right on the line between them.

24
00:01:08,299 --> 00:01:11,414
According to the federal agency that owns the

25
00:01:11,414 --> 00:01:14,321
building, about 70,000 vehicles and 20,000

26
00:01:14,321 --> 00:01:17,366
pedestrians head north through it every day.

27
00:01:17,816 --> 00:01:20,678
Commuters. Students. Shoppers. Families.

28
00:01:20,678 --> 00:01:23,469
Lines of cars stretch back into Mexico.

29
00:01:23,919 --> 00:01:26,064
Most of them have nothing to hide.

30
00:01:26,064 --> 00:01:28,967
Officers at the booths have to decide who gets

31
00:01:28,967 --> 00:01:29,850
a closer look.

32
00:01:30,300 --> 00:01:33,537
In 2022, CBP's acting field operations

33
00:01:33,537 --> 00:01:37,284
director in San Diego said her officers sift

34
00:01:37,284 --> 00:01:40,862
through about 150,000 northbound travelers

35
00:01:40,862 --> 00:01:41,713
every day.

36
00:01:42,163 --> 00:01:44,711
And somewhere in those lines, every day,

37
00:01:44,711 --> 00:01:46,558
someone is carrying fentanyl.

38
00:01:47,558 --> 00:01:49,684
Fentanyl is a synthetic opioid.

39
00:01:49,684 --> 00:01:51,672
It doesn't come from a plant.

40
00:01:51,672 --> 00:01:53,318
It comes from chemicals.

41
00:01:53,768 --> 00:01:57,096
According to the DEA, about 2 milligrams can

42
00:01:57,096 --> 00:01:58,382
be a lethal dose.

43
00:01:58,382 --> 00:02:01,559
A single gram, the size of a sugar packet,

44
00:02:01,559 --> 00:02:04,584
could potentially kill up to 500 people.

45
00:02:05,034 --> 00:02:08,589
According to the DEA, the main suppliers are

46
00:02:08,589 --> 00:02:10,204
two Mexican cartels.

47
00:02:10,204 --> 00:02:13,355
The Sinaloa Cartel, and the Jalisco New

48
00:02:13,355 --> 00:02:16,021
Generation Cartel, known as CJNG.

49
00:02:16,471 --> 00:02:19,445
The raw materials come from farther away.

50
00:02:19,445 --> 00:02:22,418
The DEA's 2025 threat assessment says the

51
00:02:22,418 --> 00:02:25,102
cartels get their precursor chemicals

52
00:02:25,102 --> 00:02:27,351
primarily from China and India.

53
00:02:27,801 --> 00:02:31,181
Pill presses turn the powder into tablets.

54
00:02:31,181 --> 00:02:34,642
In 2023, officers at New York's JFK airport

55
00:02:34,642 --> 00:02:38,666
seized 14 pill press die sets, shipped from China.

56
00:02:38,666 --> 00:02:41,966
These are the molds that stamp the pills.

57
00:02:42,416 --> 00:02:45,509
The finished pills are made to look like real

58
00:02:45,509 --> 00:02:46,815
prescription drugs.

59
00:02:46,815 --> 00:02:49,703
Many are blue tablets stamped M30, made to

60
00:02:49,703 --> 00:02:51,077
look like oxycodone.

61
00:02:51,527 --> 00:02:54,955
People who buy them often have no idea what's

62
00:02:54,955 --> 00:02:55,488
inside.

63
00:02:55,488 --> 00:02:58,763
In DEA lab testing, about 5 out of every 10

64
00:02:58,763 --> 00:03:02,343
fake pills contained a potentially deadly dose.

65
00:03:02,793 --> 00:03:03,336
The U.S.

66
00:03:03,336 --> 00:03:06,591
attorney in San Diego warned about exactly that.

67
00:03:07,591 --> 00:03:10,252
Most of it comes through the official ports of

68
00:03:10,252 --> 00:03:10,599
entry.

69
00:03:11,049 --> 00:03:14,059
In 2023, the Department of Homeland Security

70
00:03:14,059 --> 00:03:16,795
said more than 90 percent of fentanyl is

71
00:03:16,795 --> 00:03:20,148
trafficked in cars and trucks, through the ports.

72
00:03:20,148 --> 00:03:22,953
Not over the wall, but through the gates.

73
00:03:23,403 --> 00:03:27,360
CBP's own data for the first eight months of 2026:

74
00:03:27,360 --> 00:03:31,001
about 87 percent of the fentanyl it seized was

75
00:03:31,001 --> 00:03:33,771
stopped at official ports of entry.

76
00:03:34,221 --> 00:03:36,926
So the job is finding a few pounds of powder

77
00:03:36,926 --> 00:03:39,447
in a stream of tens of thousands of cars.

78
00:03:39,897 --> 00:03:41,901
It starts before the booth.

79
00:03:41,901 --> 00:03:45,239
Officers and dogs work the lines, in what CBP

80
00:03:45,239 --> 00:03:46,575
calls pre-primary.

81
00:03:47,025 --> 00:03:47,810
Then imaging.

82
00:03:47,810 --> 00:03:50,772
Large scanners can look through a vehicle's body.

83
00:03:50,772 --> 00:03:53,915
An officer looks for shapes that shouldn't be there.

84
00:03:54,365 --> 00:03:57,049
Anything suspicious goes to secondary.

85
00:03:57,049 --> 00:03:59,592
Here, officers can take a car apart.

86
00:04:00,042 --> 00:04:02,564
Smugglers build hidden compartments.

87
00:04:02,564 --> 00:04:05,787
Quarter panels. Spare tires. Seats. Gas tanks.

88
00:04:05,787 --> 00:04:06,207
Roofs.

89
00:04:06,657 --> 00:04:09,908
In June 2023, officers at San Ysidro spot

90
00:04:09,908 --> 00:04:13,238
plastic-wrapped packages in a sedan's rear

91
00:04:13,238 --> 00:04:14,427
quarter panels.

92
00:04:14,427 --> 00:04:18,074
Hidden in the panels, the dashboard, the seats

93
00:04:18,074 --> 00:04:19,421
and the gas tank:

94
00:04:19,421 --> 00:04:22,989
sixty-one packages of colored fentanyl pills.

95
00:04:22,989 --> 00:04:24,257
About 42 pounds.

96
00:04:24,707 --> 00:04:27,406
Every package is weighed, tested, and logged

97
00:04:27,406 --> 00:04:28,142
as evidence.

98
00:04:28,592 --> 00:04:31,877
Officers test the substance on the spot to

99
00:04:31,877 --> 00:04:33,285
identify the drug.

100
00:04:33,285 --> 00:04:36,884
CBP has also set up a small forward laboratory

101
00:04:36,884 --> 00:04:38,683
at the San Ysidro port.

102
00:04:39,133 --> 00:04:40,957
Then the drugs go to a vault.

103
00:04:40,957 --> 00:04:43,221
They stay there until the smuggler's

104
00:04:43,221 --> 00:04:44,730
prosecution is complete.

105
00:04:44,730 --> 00:04:46,429
After that, they're burned.

106
00:04:47,429 --> 00:04:50,121
The people in the driver's seat are usually

107
00:04:50,121 --> 00:04:51,247
not cartel bosses.

108
00:04:51,697 --> 00:04:54,860
Here is a fact that surprises many people.

109
00:04:54,860 --> 00:04:57,947
In fiscal year 2025, 84 percent of people

110
00:04:57,947 --> 00:05:01,109
sentenced in federal court for trafficking

111
00:05:01,109 --> 00:05:03,217
fentanyl were U.S. citizens.

112
00:05:03,667 --> 00:05:06,753
The typical offender was 35 years old.

113
00:05:06,753 --> 00:05:08,377
83 percent were men.

114
00:05:08,377 --> 00:05:11,219
The average sentence was 79 months.

115
00:05:11,669 --> 00:05:15,178
A CBP director in San Diego said traffickers

116
00:05:15,178 --> 00:05:18,608
use all kinds of people to avoid suspicion.

117
00:05:18,608 --> 00:05:20,203
Including teenagers.

118
00:05:20,653 --> 00:05:22,516
Remember the Ford Focus.

119
00:05:22,516 --> 00:05:26,011
The driver was Flavio Diego Rivera Davalos, a

120
00:05:26,011 --> 00:05:29,583
college student in Tijuana, who also worked as

121
00:05:29,583 --> 00:05:30,359
a teacher.

122
00:05:30,809 --> 00:05:33,677
According to prosecutors, traffickers gave him

123
00:05:33,677 --> 00:05:36,482
the car, and money to put it in his own name.

124
00:05:36,482 --> 00:05:39,475
He was told to cross the border again and again.

125
00:05:39,475 --> 00:05:42,031
Prosecutors called it burning the plates.

126
00:05:42,481 --> 00:05:45,419
The day before, he handed the car back to them

127
00:05:45,419 --> 00:05:46,825
so it could be loaded.

128
00:05:46,825 --> 00:05:49,699
On the day of his arrest, he was driving in a

129
00:05:49,699 --> 00:05:52,574
three-car caravan, and he suspected all three

130
00:05:52,574 --> 00:05:53,851
were carrying drugs.

131
00:05:54,301 --> 00:05:55,551
He pleaded guilty.

132
00:05:55,551 --> 00:05:57,772
His lawyers asked for 30 months.

133
00:05:57,772 --> 00:06:00,964
Judge Larry Burns said he did not play a minor

134
00:06:00,964 --> 00:06:03,671
role, and sentenced him to 87 months in

135
00:06:03,671 --> 00:06:04,712
federal prison.

136
00:06:05,162 --> 00:06:07,822
The judge also said he found it troubling that

137
00:06:07,822 --> 00:06:10,481
a teacher had failed to set an example for his

138
00:06:10,481 --> 00:06:11,349
young students.

139
00:06:11,799 --> 00:06:15,168
Eight months after that arrest, on August 8,

140
00:06:15,168 --> 00:06:18,460
2018, at about 2:30 in the morning, another

141
00:06:18,460 --> 00:06:20,375
car is sent to secondary.

142
00:06:20,825 --> 00:06:24,199
In its rear quarter panel, officers find about

143
00:06:24,199 --> 00:06:27,354
20,000 counterfeit pills, made to look like

144
00:06:27,354 --> 00:06:28,748
oxycodone. The U.S.

145
00:06:28,748 --> 00:06:31,683
attorney in San Diego called it likely a

146
00:06:31,683 --> 00:06:32,857
national record.

147
00:06:33,307 --> 00:06:34,745
The driver was a U.S.

148
00:06:34,745 --> 00:06:37,894
citizen who lived in Tijuana, and worked for a

149
00:06:37,894 --> 00:06:40,359
trash collection service in the U S.

150
00:06:40,359 --> 00:06:43,304
He pleaded guilty to importing the pills, a

151
00:06:43,304 --> 00:06:46,043
charge with a 10-year mandatory minimum.

152
00:06:47,043 --> 00:06:49,838
By then, San Diego was becoming the center of

153
00:06:49,838 --> 00:06:50,584
the problem.

154
00:06:51,034 --> 00:06:54,004
At the ports in the Southern District of

155
00:06:54,004 --> 00:06:57,346
California, fentanyl seizures went from about

156
00:06:57,346 --> 00:07:00,687
30 kilograms in fiscal 2015, to more than 540

157
00:07:00,687 --> 00:07:02,618
kilograms two years later.

158
00:07:03,068 --> 00:07:06,371
Between the ports, the trend was the same.

159
00:07:06,371 --> 00:07:09,910
San Diego's Border Patrol sector only started

160
00:07:09,910 --> 00:07:11,955
tracking fentanyl in 2016.

161
00:07:11,955 --> 00:07:14,865
That first year, it seized 71 pounds.

162
00:07:15,315 --> 00:07:19,038
By 2022, CBP officers and Border Patrol agents

163
00:07:19,038 --> 00:07:22,680
in San Diego and Imperial counties had seized

164
00:07:22,680 --> 00:07:25,918
about 60 percent of all the fentanyl CBP

165
00:07:25,918 --> 00:07:29,641
seized nationwide, in the first nine months of

166
00:07:29,641 --> 00:07:31,017
that fiscal year.

167
00:07:31,467 --> 00:07:33,741
And the deaths followed.

168
00:07:33,741 --> 00:07:38,101
In San Diego County, fentanyl-related overdose

169
00:07:38,101 --> 00:07:42,271
deaths went from 33 in 2016, to at least 817

170
00:07:42,271 --> 00:07:43,029
in 2021.

171
00:07:43,479 --> 00:07:46,935
Officials hung a poster at the San Ysidro and

172
00:07:46,935 --> 00:07:48,164
Otay Mesa ports.

173
00:07:48,164 --> 00:07:50,391
It read, your fentanyl kills.

174
00:07:50,841 --> 00:07:51,373
The U.S.

175
00:07:51,373 --> 00:07:54,831
attorney at the time, Randy Grossman, put it simply.

176
00:07:55,281 --> 00:07:58,721
In March 2023, Homeland Security launched a

177
00:07:58,721 --> 00:08:01,121
surge at the southwest border.

178
00:08:01,121 --> 00:08:03,921
It was called Operation Blue Lotus.

179
00:08:04,371 --> 00:08:05,389
Extra agents.

180
00:08:05,389 --> 00:08:06,563
Extra officers.

181
00:08:06,563 --> 00:08:10,557
More dogs, more scans, more cars sent to secondary.

182
00:08:11,007 --> 00:08:14,494
In one vehicle alone, officers found 116

183
00:08:14,494 --> 00:08:18,503
packages, about 163 pounds of fentanyl, hidden

184
00:08:18,503 --> 00:08:20,159
throughout the car.

185
00:08:20,609 --> 00:08:23,958
Across the Southern and Central Districts of

186
00:08:23,958 --> 00:08:27,002
California, the surge seized about 4,700

187
00:08:27,002 --> 00:08:29,970
pounds of fentanyl, and 1,700 pounds of

188
00:08:29,970 --> 00:08:31,492
precursor chemicals.

189
00:08:31,492 --> 00:08:34,156
More than 200 people were arrested.

190
00:08:34,606 --> 00:08:37,170
Grossman said what investigators had been

191
00:08:37,170 --> 00:08:38,233
seeing for years.

192
00:08:39,233 --> 00:08:42,337
Along the southwest border, in its first

193
00:08:42,337 --> 00:08:45,520
month, Blue Lotus stopped more than 4,000

194
00:08:45,520 --> 00:08:48,780
pounds of fentanyl at ports of entry, plus

195
00:08:48,780 --> 00:08:52,350
more than 3,500 pounds of methamphetamine, and

196
00:08:52,350 --> 00:08:53,825
led to 156 arrests.

197
00:08:54,275 --> 00:08:56,699
Every seizure becomes a case.

198
00:08:56,699 --> 00:08:59,123
In fiscal year 2022, the U.S.

199
00:08:59,123 --> 00:09:02,885
attorney's office in San Diego prosecuted 317

200
00:09:02,885 --> 00:09:05,309
people for fentanyl offenses.

201
00:09:05,309 --> 00:09:08,987
More than 1,800 percent more than five years

202
00:09:08,987 --> 00:09:09,656
earlier.

203
00:09:10,106 --> 00:09:11,834
The penalties are heavy.

204
00:09:11,834 --> 00:09:15,075
Importing large amounts of fentanyl can carry

205
00:09:15,075 --> 00:09:17,092
a 10-year mandatory minimum.

206
00:09:17,092 --> 00:09:20,837
If a sale leads to a death, the minimum is 20 years.

207
00:09:21,287 --> 00:09:24,351
In one case, a woman drove into San Ysidro

208
00:09:24,351 --> 00:09:27,342
with fentanyl, methamphetamine and heroin

209
00:09:27,342 --> 00:09:30,333
hidden in a spare tire under her vehicle.

210
00:09:30,333 --> 00:09:31,865
A jury convicted her.

211
00:09:31,865 --> 00:09:33,105
She got 10 years.

212
00:09:33,555 --> 00:09:36,409
In the cases in this file, the people in court

213
00:09:36,409 --> 00:09:37,464
were the drivers.

214
00:09:37,464 --> 00:09:39,635
Not the people who loaded the cars.

215
00:09:40,635 --> 00:09:42,299
And then, something changed.

216
00:09:42,749 --> 00:09:44,037
In 2024, U.S.

217
00:09:44,037 --> 00:09:48,197
overdose deaths fell by almost 27 percent,

218
00:09:48,197 --> 00:09:50,277
according to the CDC.

219
00:09:50,277 --> 00:09:53,843
From about 110,000, to about 80,000.

220
00:09:54,293 --> 00:09:57,642
The DEA reported that fentanyl purity declined

221
00:09:57,642 --> 00:09:58,806
throughout 2024.

222
00:09:58,806 --> 00:10:01,718
It linked that to cartel chemists having

223
00:10:01,718 --> 00:10:04,703
trouble getting some precursor chemicals.

224
00:10:05,153 --> 00:10:08,976
By its count, the DEA seized 61 million fake

225
00:10:08,976 --> 00:10:10,193
pills in 2024.

226
00:10:10,193 --> 00:10:13,495
24 percent fewer than the year before.

227
00:10:13,945 --> 00:10:16,777
But the drug hasn't stopped coming.

228
00:10:16,777 --> 00:10:20,418
In April 2026, at San Ysidro, a dog alerts on

229
00:10:20,418 --> 00:10:21,794
a Toyota Corolla.

230
00:10:21,794 --> 00:10:25,354
A scan leads officers to more than 14 pounds

231
00:10:25,354 --> 00:10:28,025
of fentanyl powder in its panels.

232
00:10:28,475 --> 00:10:31,760
Six days later, a scan of a Honda Pilot shows

233
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,366
something in the roof.

234
00:10:33,366 --> 00:10:36,651
About 35 pounds of fentanyl, and 80 pounds of

235
00:10:36,651 --> 00:10:37,819
methamphetamine.

236
00:10:38,269 --> 00:10:40,105
Both drivers were arrested.

237
00:10:40,105 --> 00:10:43,098
Charges are allegations, and every defendant

238
00:10:43,098 --> 00:10:46,567
is presumed innocent unless proven guilty in court.

239
00:10:47,017 --> 00:10:49,849
The port director, Mariza Marín, described

240
00:10:49,849 --> 00:10:52,073
what her officers are up against.

241
00:10:52,523 --> 00:10:56,086
Nationally, CBP seized about 7,000 pounds of

242
00:10:56,086 --> 00:10:59,568
fentanyl in the first eight months of 2026.

243
00:10:59,568 --> 00:11:03,211
Roughly the same as a year earlier. Not gone.

244
00:11:04,211 --> 00:11:07,465
2016. 2017. 2018. 2023. 2026.

245
00:11:07,465 --> 00:11:11,280
Different cars, different drivers.

246
00:11:11,280 --> 00:11:12,851
The same port.

247
00:11:13,301 --> 00:11:16,725
Every seizure is a load that never reaches a street.

248
00:11:16,725 --> 00:11:19,227
But every one also tells investigators

249
00:11:19,227 --> 00:11:20,808
something uncomfortable.

250
00:11:20,808 --> 00:11:23,968
Somebody, somewhere, expected it to get through.

251
00:11:24,418 --> 00:11:25,798
70,000 cars a day.

252
00:11:25,798 --> 00:11:27,562
A few pounds of powder.

253
00:11:27,562 --> 00:11:29,709
And a dog, walking the line.

254
00:11:30,509 --> 00:11:32,466
Case file 005. Closed.

255
00:11:32,466 --> 00:11:35,757
The next file is already on the desk.
